 "question": "why are GPU cell turns ~3.5s when eval runs at 200+ tok/s?",
 "answer": "Ollama's GPU lane (WSL /dev/dxg, 6GB) keeps one runner hot: every model switch reloads weights (load_duration ~3.5s); same-runner back-to-back queries are 0.00s load. The alternating 3-cell pair pattern pays the reload on every query. CPU-lane runners stay resident in RAM and pay no such cost.",
